---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CHECK_LABELS, REPO_URL, url } from '../lib/paths';
import { rulesByCheck } from '../lib/rules';
import { sampleReport } from '../lib/sample';
import { renderSheet } from '../lib/sheet';

const groups = rulesByCheck();
const ruleCount = (check: string) => groups.find((g) => g.check === check)?.rules.length ?? 0;
const sheet = renderSheet(sampleReport(), { ruleHref: (r) => url(`rules/${r}/`), headingLevel: 3 });
const checks = ['build', 'output', 'references', 'accessibility', 'venue'] as const;
---
<Base title="Preflight for LaTeX papers and theses" description="Overfull checks a LaTeX paper or thesis before you submit: the build log, the PDF, every reference, accessibility and venue rules. For authors working by hand or with an AI agent." section="home">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>Preflight for LaTeX papers and theses</span></p>
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-measure">
        <h1 id="hero-title"><span class="l">Write your paper</span> <span class="l l-over">with any AI agent, or by hand.<span class="slug" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="slug-note" aria-hidden="true">Overfull \hbox (14.2pt too wide) in paragraph at line 1</span></span> <span class="l">Ship one that checks out.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="lede">Overfull is a free, open preflight kit for LaTeX. It compiles your document, reads the log and the PDF, looks up every reference, and tells you what is wrong in plain language, with the file and line to fix.</p>
        <p class="hero-links">
          <a class="cta" href={url('check/')}>Check a log or PDF in your browser</a>
          <a class="caret-link" href={url('docs/')}>Read the guide</a>
        </p>
        <p class="hero-note">The browser check runs on this page; your files are not uploaded.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="hero-facts" aria-label="At a glance">
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Pre-release: v3.0.0 is not out yet</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Licence</dt><dd>MIT; templates MIT-0</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Runs on</dt><dd>Docker, or a local TeX Live 2026</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Agents</dt><dd>Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini CLI, or none</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="gap-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>What goes wrong</span></p>
    <div class="galley">
      <aside class="marginal">
        <p>Overfull never writes research content, and never calls a reference fake. It reports what the indexes say: verified, metadata differs, not found, or cannot be checked automatically.</p>
      </aside>
      <h2 id="gap-title">What goes wrong before a deadline</h2>
      <p>A citation to a paper that does not exist, or exists with a different year. <code>??</code> where a figure number should be. A figure without alt text. Ten pages when the workshop allows nine. Whether you typed the LaTeX or an agent did, these slip through on the last night, and none of them needs judgement to find: they are facts about the log, the PDF and public indexes, so a program can check them.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="specimen" aria-labelledby="specimen-cap">
      <div class="specimen-page">
        <div class="sp-row">
          <p class="sp-text">Retrieval improves proof search when the index is built from verified lemmas, as shown in Figure <span class="sp-circle">??</span> and in recent work on scaling <span class="sp-cite">[<span class="sp-circle">?</span>]</span>.</p>
          <p class="sp-note"><span class="sr-only">Proof mark: </span>ref?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sp-row">
          <div class="sp-figure" role="img" aria-label="An empty figure frame standing in for a plot"><span>Fig. 3</span></div>
          <p class="sp-note"><span class="sr-only">Proof mark: </span>no alt text</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sp-row sp-refs">
          <ol class="sp-bib" start="17">
            <li>A. Vaswani et al. Attention is all you need. <i>NeurIPS</i>, <span class="sp-ins">2017</span><span class="sp-strike">2018</span>.</li>
            <li class="sp-deleted"><span class="sp-strike">L. Chen and R. Okafor. Scaling laws for retrieval-augmented proof search. <i>ICLR</i>, 2024.</span>
              <svg class="sp-loop" viewBox="0 0 40 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 14 C 12 2, 26 2, 30 10 C 33 17, 24 21, 21 15 C 19 10, 28 5, 38 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="sp-note"><span class="sr-only">Proof marks: </span>year: 2017 (arXiv)<br />not in CrossRef, DBLP, arXiv</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sp-row sp-folio-row">
          <p class="sp-folio">10</p>
          <p class="sp-note"><span class="sr-only">Proof mark: </span>limit 9 pp.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption id="specimen-cap">A draft page as an editor would mark it. Each red note is a problem <code>overfull check</code> reports with a rule id, a location and a fix.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="ways-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>Three ways to work</span></p>
    <h2 id="ways-title" class="sr-only">Three ways to work</h2>
    <div class="ways">
      <div class="way">
        <h3>By hand</h3>
        <p>Write LaTeX the way you always have. <code>make build</code> compiles in Docker, so a local TeX Live is optional. <code>make check</code> prints the report in plain language, with the file and line of each problem.</p>
        <p><a href={url('docs/by-hand/')} class="caret-link">Working by hand</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="way">
        <h3>With an agent</h3>
        <p>The templates ship <code>AGENTS.md</code> and skills that coding agents read. The agent adds references only through <code>overfull cite</code>, which writes the entry from CrossRef, arXiv or DBLP, runs <code>overfull check --json</code> after each change, and opens a pull request you review with the changes highlighted in the PDF.</p>
        <p><a href={url('docs/with-an-agent/')} class="caret-link">Working with an agent</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="way">
        <h3>In CI</h3>
        <p>The GitHub Action reads the log, PDF and <code>.bib</code> your workflow already builds, annotates the pull request at the right lines and writes a summary. Each template also ships a workflow that builds in Docker and runs veraPDF.</p>
        <p><a href={url('docs/action/')} class="caret-link">The GitHub Action</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ways-joint">All three give the same report, and so does the browser check on this site.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="checks-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>Five checks</span></p>
    <div class="galley">
      <aside class="marginal"><p>Reports list the checks in this order. A check is <em>skipped</em>, with a reason, when its inputs are missing: no PDF yet, or offline.</p></aside>
      <h2 id="checks-title">What a check covers</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="checks">
      {checks.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <h3><a href={url(`rules/#${c}`)}>{CHECK_LABELS[c]!.name}</a></h3>
          <p>{CHECK_LABELS[c]!.blurb}</p>
          <p class="checks-count">{ruleCount(c)} rules</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="session-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>An agent session</span></p>
    <div class="galley">
      <aside class="marginal">
        <p>The agent never types a BibTeX entry. <code>overfull cite</code> fetches the record, and <code>check</code> catches anything that slipped in another way.</p>
        <p>JSON output is the <code>Report</code> type: stable rule ids, locations and fixes.</p>
      </aside>
      <h2 id="session-title">Cite, check, fix, repeat</h2>
      <p>A workshop paper, a nine-page limit, one request. This is the loop the template’s instructions put an agent in.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="transcript" aria-label="Example agent session">
      <p class="t-you"><span class="t-who">you</span><span class="t-say">Add the Vaswani et al. transformer paper to related work. We need to stay under the 9-page limit.</span></p>
      <p class="t-agent"><span class="t-who">agent</span><span class="t-say">I’ll look the paper up instead of writing the entry from memory.</span></p>
      <pre class="t-cmd" tabindex="0"><span class="t-ps">$</span> overfull cite arXiv:1706.03762
<span class="t-out">found  arXiv 1706.03762  Attention Is All You Need
       Vaswani, Shazeer, Parmar, Uszkoreit, Jones, Gomez, Kaiser, Polosukhin (2017)
added  vaswani2017attention → references.bib</span></pre>
      <p class="t-agent"><span class="t-who">agent</span><span class="t-say">Cited it in <code>sections/related.tex</code> as <code>\citet&#123;vaswani2017attention&#125;</code>. Building and checking.</span></p>
      <pre class="t-cmd" tabindex="0"><span class="t-ps">$</span> overfull build && overfull check --json
<span class="t-out">&#123; "status": "fail", "checks": [ …
  &#123; "check": "venue", "status": "fail", "problems": [
    &#123; "rule": "page-limit-exceeded", "severity": "error",
      "message": "Main text runs to page 10; the limit is 9",
      "location": &#123; "page": 10 &#125; &#125; ] &#125; ] &#125;</span></pre>
      <p class="t-agent"><span class="t-who">agent</span><span class="t-say">Over by about half a page. Table 3 floats onto page 10. I’ll move the per-dataset rows to the appendix and keep the summary row in the main text.</span></p>
      <pre class="t-cmd" tabindex="0"><span class="t-ps">$</span> overfull build && overfull check
<span class="t-out">build          pass
output         pass
references     pass   32 of 32 verified
accessibility  pass   tagged, PDF/UA-2
venue          pass   main text ends on page 9 of 9</span></pre>
      <p class="t-agent"><span class="t-who">agent</span><span class="t-say">All five checks pass. Opened pull request #42, “Cite Vaswani et al.; move Table 3 detail to appendix”, with the report and a PDF showing the changes.</span></p>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="report-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>The report</span></p>
    <div class="report-grid">
      <div>
        <h2 id="report-title">One sheet per build</h2>
        <p>Every problem carries a rule id, a location and a fix. Log cascades fold under their root cause, so one missing brace is one problem, not forty.</p>
        <p>The same report comes out as terminal text, JSON for agents, Markdown for pull request comments, and GitHub annotations.</p>
        <p><a class="caret-link" href={url('check/')}>Make one from your own files</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="report-sheet" set:html={sheet} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="templates-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>Templates</span></p>
    <div class="galley">
      <aside class="marginal"><p>All three use LuaLaTeX, biblatex and TeX Live 2026, and are licensed MIT-0: copy them, owe nothing.</p></aside>
      <h2 id="templates-title">Start from a template</h2>
      <p>The thesis and paper templates produce tagged PDF/UA-2; Beamer slides cannot be tagged yet. Each template sets its language and title, requires alt text on figures, and ships agent instructions, a Makefile and a CI workflow. A fresh copy builds without errors; the paper template warns until you write its AI-use statement.</p>
      <dl class="tpl-list">
        <dt>Thesis</dt><dd>Bachelor’s, master’s and PhD. A4, chapters, front matter, PDF/UA-2. <code>overfull init thesis</code></dd>
        <dt>Paper</dt><dd>Research papers and preprints, with a page-limit marker and arXiv packaging. <code>overfull init paper</code></dd>
        <dt>Slides</dt><dd>Beamer for defences and conference talks. <code>overfull init slides</code></dd>
      </dl>
      <p><a class="caret-link" href={url('templates/')}>What is in each template</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <p class="runhead"><span>Getting started</span></p>
    <div class="galley">
      <aside class="marginal">
        <p><span class="mark">Pre-release.</span> v3.0.0 is not released yet, so the Docker image on ghcr.io, the release download and the Action’s <code>@v3</code> tag do not exist yet. The steps here use a clone, which works today.</p>
      </aside>
      <h2 id="start-title">Start in five minutes</h2>
      <p>You need Git, Node.js 22.12+, pnpm and Docker. The first build makes a TeX Live image of about 3 GB; after that, builds take seconds.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <p>Get Overfull and build its Docker image.</p>
          <div class="cmd" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Commands for step 1"><span class="p">$ </span>git clone https://github.com/amet13/overfull.git && cd overfull
<span class="p">$ </span>pnpm install && pnpm build
<span class="p">$ </span>make image IMAGE=overfull:dev</div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>Create a project from a template.</p>
          <div class="cmd" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Commands for step 2"><span class="p">$ </span>node packages/cli/dist/bin.js init paper ../my-paper && cd ../my-paper</div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>Build and check it. Or open the folder in your coding agent and ask for the change you want; it runs the check itself.</p>
          <div class="cmd" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Commands for step 3"><span class="p">$ </span>make build IMAGE=overfull:dev
<span class="p">$ </span>make check IMAGE=overfull:dev</div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h3 class="after-title">After v3.0.0</h3>
      <p>Install the single-file <code>overfull</code> download from GitHub Releases, or use only Docker with the image <code>ghcr.io/amet13/overfull:3</code>. The steps shrink to <code>overfull init paper my-paper</code>, <code>make build</code>, <code>make check</code>, and CI to <code>uses: amet13/overfull@v3</code>.</p>
      <p>Already have a LaTeX project and a build log? <a href={url('check/')}>Check it in your browser</a> now. Source and issues are on <a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ----- Hero: the one bold overfull rule ----- */
  .hero {
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .hero-measure {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }
  /* Crop mark at the top-left corner of the text block */
  .hero-measure::after {
    content: none;
    position: absolute;
    left: -0.9rem;
    top: 0.35rem;
    width: 0.6rem;
    height: 0.6rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--hair-strong);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair-strong);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.3rem + 3.4vw, var(--s4));
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  }
  .slug,
  .slug-note {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .hero-measure::after {
      content: '';
    }
    .hero h1 .l {
      display: block;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    /* The line that does not fit: it runs past the dashed right margin, and
       draft mode marks it with a black rule, exactly as LaTeX does. */
    .l-over {
      position: relative;
      width: max-content;
    }
    .l-over::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      right: 0.78em;
      top: -1.6em;
      bottom: -1.6em;
      border-right: 1px dashed var(--guide);
    }
    .slug {
      display: inline-block;
      width: 0.28em;
      height: 0.72em;
      margin-left: 0.1em;
      background: var(--slug);
      vertical-align: -0.02em;
      transform-origin: left center;
      animation: overrun 900ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1) 350ms both;
    }
  }
  @keyframes overrun {
    from {
      transform: scaleX(0);
    }
    to {
      transform: scaleX(1);
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1100px) {
    .slug-note {
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      left: calc(100% + 1.5rem);
      top: 0.1em;
      width: 12rem;
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      font-weight: 400;
      letter-spacing: 0;
      white-space: normal;
      line-height: 1.4;
      color: var(--pencil);
      animation: note-in 400ms ease-out 1200ms both;
    }
  }
  @keyframes note-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }
  .hero-text {
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .hero-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5em;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 1.1rem 0.5rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    font-size: var(--s0);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .cta::before {
    content: '‸';
    color: var(--pencil);
    font-variant-caps: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
    filter: brightness(1.6);
  }
  .cta:hover {
    background: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .hero-note {
    font-size: var(--s-1);
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .hero-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem 2rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--s-1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }
  .hero-facts div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .hero-facts dt {
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .hero-facts dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .hero-facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
    .hero-facts div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.1rem;
      align-content: start;
    }
  }

  /* ----- Specimen: a marked-up proof ----- */
  .specimen {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + var(--margin-w) + var(--gap));
  }
  .specimen-page {
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--hair-strong);
    padding: 1.5rem clamp(0.9rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    font-size: var(--s-1);
    position: relative;
  }
  .sp-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) clamp(6rem, 24%, 11rem);
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
    border-right: 0;
  }
  .sp-text {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    text-align: left;
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .sp-text {
      text-align: justify;
      hyphens: auto;
    }
  }
  .sp-note {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--s-1);
    color: var(--pencil);
    line-height: 1.3;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--pencil);
    padding-left: 0.5rem;
  }
  .sp-circle {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0 0.2em;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--pencil);
    border-radius: 50%;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .sp-figure {
    height: 5.5rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--hair-strong);
    display: grid;
    place-items: end start;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, transparent 0 9px, var(--paper-2) 9px 10px);
  }
  .sp-bib {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 2em;
    font-size: var(--s-1);
  }
  .sp-bib li {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
  .sp-strike {
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-color: var(--pencil);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1.5px;
  }
  .sp-ins {
    color: var(--pencil);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-right: 0.25em;
  }
  .sp-ins::before {
    content: '‸';
  }
  .sp-deleted {
    position: relative;
  }
  .sp-loop {
    width: 2.3rem;
    height: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--pencil);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .sp-folio {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-variant-numeric: oldstyle-nums;
  }
  .sp-folio-row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
    padding-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .specimen figcaption {
    font-size: var(--s-1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  /* ----- Three ways ----- */
  .ways {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem;
  }
  .way h3 {
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .way p {
    font-size: var(--s-1);
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .ways {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
    .way + .way {
      border-left: 1px solid var(--hair);
      padding-left: 2.5rem;
    }
  }
  .ways-joint {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  /* ----- Checks: ordered, because reports use this order ----- */
  .checks {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: chk;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + var(--margin-w) + var(--gap));
  }
  .checks li {
    counter-increment: chk;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.4rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    column-gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .checks li::before {
    content: counter(chk);
    grid-row: 1 / span 3;
    font-size: var(--s3);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--pencil);
    font-variant-numeric: oldstyle-nums;
  }
  .checks h3 {
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    font-size: var(--s1);
  }
  .checks h3 a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .checks h3 a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--pencil);
  }
  .checks p {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  }
  .checks-count {
    font-size: var(--s-1);
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .checks li {
      grid-template-columns: 2.4rem 11rem minmax(0, 1fr) 5rem;
      align-items: baseline;
    }
    .checks li::before {
      grid-row: auto;
    }
    .checks p {
      margin: 0;
    }
    .checks-count {
      text-align: right;
    }
  }

  /* ----- Transcript ----- */
  .transcript {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    background: var(--code-paper);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--guide);
